# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents (and humans) working in **{{.Name}}** — {{if eq .ProjectType "api"}}an{{else}}a{{end}} `{{.ProjectType}}` project scaffolded by [Gopamin](https://github.com/bezmoradi/gopamin) using the Clean Architecture (Ports & Adapters) pattern. This file follows the [AGENTS.md](https://agents.md) convention.

## What this project is

{{if $isRest -}}
A JSON REST API built on the **{{.Platform}}** HTTP framework. It exposes a `User` resource under `/api/v1/users` behind a consistent JSON envelope — see [HTTP API](#http-api).
{{- else if $isGraphql -}}
A **GraphQL** API (graphql-go) exposing a `User` schema over a single `/graphql` endpoint — see [GraphQL API](#graphql-api).
{{- else if $isWeb -}}
A server-rendered **web application** on the **{{.Platform}}** HTTP framework: it renders HTML pages for a `User` resource and serves embedded CSS. The binary is self-contained — HTML/CSS are embedded via `//go:embed` — see [Web UI](#web-ui).
{{- else if $isWorker -}}
A **broker-driven worker** with no HTTP server. It connects to **{{.Broker}}**, publishes a sample message on startup, and consumes messages in a loop until interrupted — see [Broker workflow](#broker-workflow).
{{- else -}}
A minimal **hello-world** starter that demonstrates the Clean Architecture layout{{if $hasRealDB}} with a durable `{{.Database}}` repository{{end}}. Grow it by following the [dependency rule](#the-dependency-rule).
{{- end}}

